WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Client SYN uses sequence 1000 and consumes one sequence number.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Server SYN-ACK uses its own sequence 5000 and acknowledges 1001.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Client ACK acknowledges 5001. Client data will start at 1001.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
500 bytes starting at 1001 end at 1500.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Cumulative ACK 1501 means that byte 1501 is next expected.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.700
1001 plus 500 equals 1501. TCP counts bytes, not packets.
